english_question:
In the figure, in parallelogram ABCD, ∠ABD = 30°, AB = 4, AE ⊥ BD, CF ⊥ BD, and points E and F are exactly the trisection points of BD. M and N are the midpoints of AB and CD, respectively. What is the area of quadrilateral MENF?
A. 3 \sqrt{3}
B. \sqrt{3}
C. 3 \sqrt{2}
D. \sqrt{2}

A square ABCD with a side length of 1 is folded along the diagonal BD, connecting AC to form the triangular pyramid C-ABD. The front view and top view are congruent isosceles right triangles, as shown in the figure. What is the area of the side view? ( )
A. \frac{1}{4}
B. \frac{1}{2}
C. \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
D. 1

In quadrilateral ABCD, it is known that AB = BC = CD, and angles ∠BAD and ∠CDA are acute. Point F is a point on diagonal BD, EF is parallel to AB and intersects AD at point E, FG is parallel to BC and intersects DC at point G. Quadrilateral EFGP is a parallelogram. The following conclusions are given: 
① Quadrilateral EFGP is a rhombus; 
② Triangle PED is an isosceles triangle; 
③ If ∠ABD = 90°, then triangle EFP is congruent to triangle GPD; 
④ If quadrilateral FPDG is also a parallelogram, then BC is parallel to AD and ∠CDA = 60°. 
Which of the following conclusions are correct? (Fill in all the correct conclusion numbers in the blank).

In the circle O, the degree measure of angle AOB is m. Point C is a point on arc ACB, and points D and E are two different points on arc AB (not coinciding with points A and B). What is the degree measure of angle D + angle E?
A. m
B. 180° - \frac{m}{2}
C. 90° + \frac{m}{2}
D. \frac{m}{2}

The three views of the spatial geometric body are shown in the figure, then the surface area of this spatial geometric body is ( )
A. 32+10 \sqrt{10}
B. 20+5 \sqrt{10}
C. 57
D. 42
